{{!-- THE WHOLE CELL IS THE ROLL, and always was: the `<li>` carries `.rollable` and the stat
      key, so a click anywhere on it — the label, the box, the abbreviation — rolls that stat.
      The dice icon that used to sit in front of the label was decoration on top of that, and
      is gone; nothing about what rolls changed with it.

      The value input is `readonly` outside edit mode, which is what lets a click on the number
      itself fall through to the roll (the sheet's rollable handler steps aside for an ENABLED,
      writable input, so in edit mode the same click types instead).

      A BOX THE RULES CAN'T ACCOUNT FOR wears a caution frame and carries the sentence saying
      why. Nothing is blocked: any number can be typed and it is what the sheet keeps and what
      the dice add. `stonetop.statIssues` is built only while this section is being edited (see
      StonetopCharacterSheet's getData and stat-rules.js), so a sheet being played from never
      carries the frame and the lookup below is empty on every other render.

      The tooltip hangs on the BOX rather than the `<li>`, which is deliberate: the cell already
      takes a hover description of the stat itself (applyLabelTooltips, gated on its own client
      setting), and the nearest `[data-tooltip]` under the pointer is the one that shows. So the
      caution is on the thing wearing the caution frame, and the description stays on the label
      and the abbreviation either side of it. --}}
<div class="cell--stats">
	<ul class="stats-list">
	{{#each system.stats}}
	<li class="stat cell--stat rollable" data-stat="{{@key}}" data-roll="{{@key}}">
		<span class="cell__title">{{statLabel @key}}</span>
		<div class="stonetop-stat-box{{#if (lookup @root.stonetop.statIssues @key)}} stonetop-stat-box--off-rules{{/if}}"
		     {{~#with (lookup @root.stonetop.statIssues @key)}} data-tooltip="{{message}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN"{{/with}}>
			<div class="stonetop-stat-inner">
				<input class="stat-value" type="number"
				       name="system.stats.{{@key}}.value"
				       value="{{value}}"
				       {{#unless @root.stonetop.statsEdit}}readonly{{/unless}}>
			</div>
		</div>
		<span class="stonetop-stat-abbr">({{@key}})</span>
	</li>
	{{/each}}
	</ul>
</div>
